   "subject": "Count and relative frequencies in dataframe by multiple criteria",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Hello,</p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">I have a dataframe (~750,000 rows) containing records of\r\nindividuals (TransmitterSerial) detected by different receivers (Receiver) over\r\na period of many months. </p>\r\n\r\n<pre style=\"line-height:11.25pt;background:white;word-break:break-all\"><span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:blue\"><br>&gt; </span></span><span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:blue\">head(df)</span></span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black\"></span></pre>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:11.25pt;background:white;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black;border:none windowtext 1.0pt;padding:0cm\"> <span>     </span>Receiver TransmitterSerial<span>       </span>Date<span>    \r\n</span>Time Hour Month</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:11.25pt;background:white;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black;border:none windowtext 1.0pt;padding:0cm\">1 VR2W-123227<span>           </span>1168793 08/07/2016 14:06:19<span>   </span>14<span>  \r\n</span>Jul</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:11.25pt;background:white;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black;border:none windowtext 1.0pt;padding:0cm\">2 VR2W-123227<span>           </span>1168793 08/07/2016 14:08:23<span>   </span>14<span>  \r\n</span>Jul</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:11.25pt;background:white;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black;border:none windowtext 1.0pt;padding:0cm\">3 VR2W-123228<span>           </span>1168793 08/07/2016 14:08:29<span>   </span>14<span>  \r\n</span>Jul</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:11.25pt;background:white;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black;border:none windowtext 1.0pt;padding:0cm\">4 VR2W-123228<span>           </span>1212923 08/07/2016 14:08:46<span>   </span>14<span>  \r\n</span>Jul</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:11.25pt;background:white;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black;border:none windowtext 1.0pt;padding:0cm\">5 VR2W-123228<span>           </span>1212923 08/07/2016 14:09:39<span>   </span>14<span>  \r\n</span>Jul</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:0cm;margin-bottom:.0001pt;line-height:11.25pt;background:white;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black;border:none windowtext 1.0pt;padding:0cm\">6 VR2W-123227<span>           </span>1168793 08/07/2016 14:11:24<span>   </span>14<span>  \r\n</span>Jul</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black\"></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> </p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">I’m trying to summarize the relative frequency of each\r\nreceiver per individual within hour (HOUR) for each day (DATE). </p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">The requested output (let it be summary_df), would ideally\r\nlook something like this:</p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;line-height:107%\"><br></span></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;line-height:107%\">&gt; </span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:blue\">head(summary_df)</span></span><span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;line-height:107%;color:blue\"></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black;border:none windowtext 1.0pt;padding:0cm\">TransmitterSerial <span> </span>Receiver<span>     </span>Date<span>    \r\n</span><span>     </span>Hour<span>     </span>count<span>  \r\n</span>relative_freq</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black;border:none windowtext 1.0pt;padding:0cm\">1168793<span>            </span>VR2W-123227\r\n<span> </span>08/07/2016<span>    </span>21<span>      \r\n</span>45<span>      </span>0.45</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black;border:none windowtext 1.0pt;padding:0cm\">1168793<span>            </span>VR2W-885115\r\n<span> </span>08/07/2016<span>    </span>21<span>      \r\n</span>6<span>      </span><span> </span>0.06</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black;border:none windowtext 1.0pt;padding:0cm\">1168793<span>            </span>VR2W-320024<span>  </span>08/07/2016<span>   \r\n</span>21<span>       </span>49<span>      </span>0.49<span>         </span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black;border:none windowtext 1.0pt;padding:0cm\">1168793<span>            </span>VR2W-123227\r\n<span> </span>08/07/2016<span>    </span>22<span>      \r\n</span>147<span>     </span>0.98</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black;border:none windowtext 1.0pt;padding:0cm\">1168793<span>            </span>VR2W-320024<span>  </span>08/07/2016<span>   \r\n</span>22<span>       </span>3<span>     </span><span> </span><span> </span>0.02</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;line-height:107%;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black;border:none windowtext 1.0pt;padding:0cm\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">I tried using dplyr to group_by(TransmitterSerial, Receiver,\r\nDate, Hour) and mutate() to count nrow() per hour and calculate relative_freq by\r\ndivision, but I keep on getting lost in the syntax. <span> </span><span> </span>I also\r\ntried a for loop to first subset by individual, but no success there either.</p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> </p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Any help would be greatly appreciated, thank you.</p>\r\n\r\n</div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "g2NbnMXHAAAJ",
   "from": "Michael Dorman",
   "author": "c0e822e430c1a5a7",
   "date": "2018-05-27T10:58:35Z",
   "subject": "Re: [Israel RUG] Count and relative frequencies in dataframe by multiple criteria",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>The general approach may be something like this - </div><div><br></div><div>1. Calculating summary table A, with N = <u>total</u> number of observations per (<u>TransmitterSerial</u>, <u>Date</u>, <u>Hour</u>), using &#39;group_by&#39; with &#39;summarize&#39;</div><div>2. Calculating summary table B, with n = number of observations per <span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.8px;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial;float:none;display:inline\">(<u>TransmitterSerial</u>, <u>Receiver</u>, <u>Date</u>, <u>Hour</u>), again using &#39;group_by&#39; with &#39;summarize&#39;</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.8px;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial;float:none;display:inline\">3. Using &#39;left_join(B, A)&#39; to get a table with both the individual count &#39;n&#39; and total hourly count &#39;N&#39;</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.8px;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial;float:none;display:inline\">4. Dividing the columns &#39;n&#39; / &#39;N&#39;, to get a new &#39;proportion&#39; column</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.8px;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial;float:none;display:inline\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.8px;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial;float:none;display:inline\">There are surely shorter ways to do it with &#39;dplyr&#39;, but this is the easiest to explain without a specific data example. </span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:12.8px;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial;float:none;display:inline\"><br></span></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Sun, May 27, 2018 at 12:27 PM, Renanel Pickholtz <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">renan...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div>"
